---
lane: parallels-{{HOST}}
producer: Parallels guest VMs on {{HOST}}, pulled by the host
host: {{HOST}}
mission: >
  The Linux VMs on this Mac hold Claude Code and Claude Desktop sessions for work the
  owner keeps in its own machine (one VM per client context). They have no SSH and no
  Tailscale, so the hub cannot reach them; the host pulls each running guest's Claude
  Code memory and Claude Desktop outputs through Parallels' own command line, one folder
  per guest. Provenance is the guest folder name; a guest's identity context travels
  with it (see knowledge/concepts/identities).
write: rsync{{WRITE_VIA}}
read: none (contribute-only, owner decision 2026-09-22)
gear: ask-first
status: onboarded
onboarded: {{DATE}}
---

Installed by `sov connect parallels` on {{DATE}}.

Write wire: `connectors/harness/parallels/mirror.sh` every {{INTERVAL}}s via {{SCHEDULER}}
(`{{RUNNER}}`, lane id `{{LABEL}}`). For every guest `prlctl list` reports as running, it
tars `/home/*/.claude/projects/*/memory/` and `/home/*/Claude/` out of the guest into
`<guest-slug>/claude-code/memory/<project>/` and `<guest-slug>/claude/`. A guest that is
stopped or suspended is named in `MANIFEST.md` and skipped; nothing is invented for it.
Credentials and transcripts are never asked for. The guest is never written to.

Read wire: none, by owner decision (2026-09-22): the guests are contribute-only. Nothing
in a guest reads the archive, and the vault is never mounted or shared into a guest.
This is the same standing as the contribute-only producer boxes, not a gap to close.
